    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 40,
      "text": "In Dinesh Tiwari vs. State of UP - (2014) 13 SCC 137 , it is held that on perusal of record and hearing the parties, at the stage of discharge under section 227 of the IPC, if the Judge is of the opinion that there is ground for presuming that the accused has committed offence, he is competent to frame charge for such offence even if not mentioned in the charge sheet.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PRE_RELIED",
